Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the DualSense's speaker over USB (TODO 216)

Over USB a DualSense is also a sound card ("Wireless Controller", 4 channels: 1-2 audio, 3-4 the actuators). While
the game wants its speaker (setSpeakerWanted) the device thread starts a WASAPI shared-mode stream to that device
(found by its name) on a thread of its own: the game's sound for the speaker, left + right on channel 2, the other
channels silent, a 20 ms cushion first. The 0x02 output report then routes the audio to the built-in speaker
(OutputState::speakerRoute: valid_flag0 0x01|0x10|0x20|0x80 - bit 1 would take the actuators out of audio mode -,
volumes, output path 0x30 = the right channel on the speaker, audio control 2 = the speaker's pre-gain; our earlier
launcher's USB bytes). No device, another format, a failure: no USB speaker, the game's sound stays on the PC.
speakerUsbLatencyMs: how long after the mix the pad is heard (the cushion, the buffer, the stream's latency,
measured at the start; -1 otherwise), for the game's Surround delay. Both transports now drop the speaker's queue
back to its cushion when it runs 100 ms over (the pad's clock and the PC's drift apart). Links ole32.

